course: dictionary
lesson: 2172
title: The word correctly
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word correctly tells you how something is done. It means in the right way, without mistakes. In «Pupils answer questions correctly», correctly tells you every answer is right. Ask yourself how the action happens, and you will find the meaning.
explain: Correctly has a second meaning about manners and rules. It can mean in a proper or polite way that fits the rules or the situation. Think of «wearing a seatbelt correctly», which means wearing it the way the rules say, so it keeps you safe.
explain: Check the meaning by swapping in a word. In «play the tricky bar slowly and correctly», the phrase "in the right way, without mistakes" still makes sense, so that meaning fits. Also notice «if I remember correctly», which shows the speaker is not completely sure.
fact: Correctly means in the right way, without mistakes.
fact: Correctly can also mean in a proper or polite way that fits the rules or the situation.
fact: Correctly is an adverb: it tells you how something is done, as in «spell words correctly».
fact: «Archerfish aim correctly» means they aim in the right way and hit their target.
fact: Useful phrases: answer correctly, spell correctly, if I remember correctly.
exercise: «Only a globe can show the shapes, areas, distances and directions of all places correctly at the same time.» What does correctly mean here? | Quickly and loudly | Very far away | In a sad way | *In the right way, without mistakes
exercise: «Archerfish ... aim correctly even though water bends light.» What does aim correctly tell you? | *They hit the insect they were aiming at | They close their eyes | They sing to the insects | They swim away from the insect
exercise: Tom greets his teacher in a proper, polite way that fits the school rules. Which word does this sentence show? | *Correctly | Quickly | Carelessly | Loudly
test: What does «if I remember correctly» show? | The speaker has forgotten everything | The speaker is very angry | The speaker is shouting | *The speaker is not completely sure
test: Ella says «I use punctuation correctly» in her essay. What does it mean? | Ella writes in a loud voice | Ella uses lots of marks everywhere | *Ella puts the marks in the right places, without mistakes | Ella writes slowly and sadly
exam: Which sentence uses correctly to mean "in the right way, without mistakes"? | Alex was given a reward for something | Ben ran to the shop after school | *Pupils spell the words correctly in the spelling test | The children sang the words loudly
